1
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:24,260
An American horror story.

2
00:10:36,521 --> 00:10:42,521
The Apprentice is a history, drama film directed by Ali Abbasi.

3
00:15:54,782 --> 00:16:00,782
A young Donald Trump, eager to make his name as a hungry scion of a wealthy family in 1970s New York, comes under
the spell of Roy Cohn, the cutthroat attorney who would help create the Donald Trump we know today.

4
00:21:13,043 --> 00:21:19,043
Cohn sees in Trump the perfect protégé—someone with raw ambition, a hunger
for success, and a willingness to do whatever it takes to win.

5
00:26:31,304 --> 00:26:37,304
Donald Trump, played by Sebastian Stan.

6
00:31:49,565 --> 00:31:55,565
Roy Cohn, played by Jeremy Strong.

7
00:37:07,826 --> 00:37:13,826
Fred Trump, played by Martin Donovan.

8
00:42:26,086 --> 00:42:32,086
Ivana Trump, played by Maria Bakalova.

9
00:47:44,347 --> 00:47:50,347
Mary Anne Trump, played by Catherine McNally.

10
00:53:02,608 --> 00:53:08,608
Freddy Trump, played by Charlie Carrick.

11
00:58:20,869 --> 00:58:26,869
The Apprentice is a 2024 independent biographical drama film
starring Sebastian Stan as President Donald Trump.

12
01:03:39,130 --> 01:03:45,130
The plot examines Trump making a career as a real estate businessman in New York City in
the 1970s and 1980s, highlighting his relationship with attorney Roy Cohn.

13
01:08:57,391 --> 01:09:03,391
Directed by Ali Abbasi and written by Gabriel Sherman, the film also stars Jeremy Strong as Cohn,
Martin Donovan as Trump's father Fred, and Maria Bakalova as Trump's first wife, Ivana.

14
01:14:15,652 --> 01:14:21,652
An international co-production between Canada, Denmark, Ireland, and the United States, the biopic was
announced in May 2018, but languished until Abbasi, Stan, and Strong joined in 2023.

15
01:19:33,913 --> 01:19:39,913
It premiered at the 77th Cannes Film Festival on May 20, 2024, and impressed the critics,
sparking an eight-minute standing ovation, and "feverish media attention".

16
01:24:52,173 --> 01:24:58,173
However, the film struggled to find American distribution due to its subject
matter and an attempt by Trump's legal team to block its release.

17
01:30:10,434 --> 01:30:16,434
Briarcliff eventually bought the rights, and
theatrically released it on October 11, 2024.

18
01:35:28,695 --> 01:35:34,695
The film underperformed at the box office, grossing $17
million worldwide on a $16 million budget.

19
01:40:46,956 --> 01:40:52,956
The film received praise from critics for its acting, directing, and editing; Trump himself, meanwhile, described it as a
"defamatory, politically disgusting hatchet job" intended to harm his ultimately successful 2024 presidential campaign.

20
01:46:05,217 --> 01:46:11,217
For their performances, Stan and Strong each received wide acclaim and recognition, including
respective nominations for Lead Actor and Supporting Actor at the 97th Academy Awards.

21
01:51:23,478 --> 01:51:29,478
The film explores themes of new york city, rape, corruption, aids, funeral.

22
01:56:41,739 --> 01:56:47,739
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
